Code in this directory derived from Linux i915 (MIT)
====================================================

Origin: Linux 6.1.176, drivers/gpu/drm/i915, from Debian's linux-source-6.1
(6.1.176-1) package, extracted 2026-11-08. Only files whose SPDX identifier is
MIT are used. Nothing GPL-licensed is copied; dma-fence/dma-resv/sync_file are
implemented fresh in Ranix with the same API.

Copied unchanged (SPDX MIT, Copyright Intel Corporation):
  i915_reg_defs.h
  gt/intel_gt_regs.h
  gt/intel_engine_regs.h
  gt/intel_gpu_commands.h
  gt/intel_lrc_reg.h

Derived (changed) code:
  ranix_gt.c
    - set_offsets(), gen9_rcs_offsets[] and the body of __lrc_init_regs() /
      init_common_regs() / __reset_stop_ring() from gt/intel_lrc.c, specialised
      to Gen9 RCS and a GGTT-only (32-bit legacy, no PPGTT) context;
      BUILD_BUG_ON_ZERO checks dropped from the table macros.
    - the forcewake get sequence (ack clear, request, ack set, fallback toggle
      WaRsForcewakeAddDelayForAck) from intel_uncore.c, rewritten over plain MMIO.
    - enable_execlists() and the ELSP write order from
      gt/intel_execlists_submission.c, the descriptor layout from lrc_descriptor().
    - the request emitters from gt/gen8_engine_cs.c: gen8_emit_flush_rcs()
      (EMIT_INVALIDATE with the Gen9 null PIPE_CONTROL), gen8_emit_bb_start(),
      gen8_emit_fini_breadcrumb_rcs() + gen8_emit_fini_breadcrumb_tail() +
      gen8_emit_wa_tail(), written into a local command array.
    - bdw_setup_private_ppat() from gt/intel_gtt.c (the PPAT values).
    - reset_csb_pointers() and a reduced process_csb() from
      gt/intel_execlists_submission.c (CSB in the HWSP, read-pointer update).
    - GT frequency (RPS) from gt/intel_rps.c: gen6_rps_get_freq_caps() (Gen9 BC
      RP_STATE_CAP fields, x GEN9_FREQ_SCALER), gen9_rps_enable() (RC_VIDEO_FREQ,
      RP_IDLE_HYSTERSIS), rps_set_power() at HIGH_POWER (EI/thresholds, RP_CONTROL
      bits), gen6_rps_set() (GEN9_FREQUENCY request), and the rps_timer()/rps_work()
      policy (95 %/85 % busy, doubling step, waitboost) reduced to one engine sampled
      on the timer tick; the RP1 boost target and 100 ms idle drop are Ranix's.
    Everything else in ranix_gt.c (objects, GGTT binding, the request queue and
    its one-at-a-time ELSP policy, kernel-context parking, hang detection and the
    wedge path, the sysfs control) is Ranix's own; ranix_power.c and
    intel_display.c (display back end, GGTT window, written from the PRM) are Ranix's own.

  ranix_gem.c
    - ioc_getparam() follows i915_getparam.c: the same parameter set, the
      "always 1" group and the rejected UMS params; values are Kaby Lake GT2's
      and what Ranix implements. The rest of the file (GEM uAPI, contexts,
      execbuffer, query, per-file address space) is Ranix's own.

  ranix_vm.c
    - PPGTT entry encoding (present|rw, PPAT_CACHED for objects, index 0 for
      directories) as in gt/gen8_ppgtt.c and gt/intel_gtt.h; the page-table
      walker is Ranix's own.

  ranix_i915_uapi.h
    - transcription of the i915 uAPI (include/uapi/drm/i915_drm.h) structs and
      numbers Ranix implements; layouts checked against that header.

The LinuxKPI headers these files compile against are in ../../linuxkpi
(BSD-2-Clause, written for Ranix).

